+# Preserve our preliminary error separately from the source
+
+The initial full-page reading of FBI-SEP01 physical 46 mistakenly treated the air-side TERMINATION DIRECTION digit as 1. A progress message therefore incorrectly reported an internal 1/1 conflict. That preliminary analyst claim is preserved here and must not be reused as a source finding.
+
+A 280 dpi crop rendered directly from the same unchanged PDF shows **0 = air; 1 = ground**. The paragraph also prints termination type 0 = normal / 1 = abnormal. This is a reading correction after a controlled closer inspection, not a historical source amendment or an adjudication of native ACIS behavior. The original low-resolution render and validation crop remain preserved locally. The ordinary extracted OCR also favored 0, but was noisy and did not control the image reading.
+
+The public source remains SHA-256 4760de107bef3c75f4d7629f90f7a70d2c861cb3b53dcbe37a3bf0fb768f93cb. The validation-crop hash is recorded in VERIFICATION.json from the saved render receipt. Do not confuse source-image certainty about a glyph with vendor implementation, a call-specific disposition or historical authentication.
+
+The prior mirror report's padded footer transcription 000000736 and a current preliminary reading 00000736 remain a separate unadopted prefix-count question. No high-resolution footer comparison was performed in this unit. Physical page 69 and suffix 736 suffice to locate the record; the uncertain padding is not evidence of alteration.
